    two that matter most — [1mmidnight rollover[0m (same task, [38;5;153mnow[39m at 23:59 vs 00:01 next day, asserting today→overdue) and
    [1mmonth/year boundaries[0m.
  - [1m[38;5;153mstore.js[0m — round-trip, absent key, malformed JSON, non-array value, array containing junk entries, and a
    save-failure path with a throwing localStorage stub.
  - [1m[38;5;153mtask.js[0m — validation accept/reject cases.
  - [1m[38;5;153mui.js[39m / [38;5;153mmain.js[0m — no unit tests. They're wiring and DOM; testing them via jsdom would cost more than it catches at
    this size. I'd rather say that outright than write hollow tests.

  First test written before implementation, TDD from there.

  That's the full design. If this looks right I'll write it up as a spec at
  [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/specs/2026-09-16-task-due-date-reminders-design.md[39m for you to review — still no code until you've
  read it.

